\n49.922848 + 64.205340 = 114.128188\n114.128188 - 47.080857 = 67.047331\nCCC \u2248 67.05 days\n\n## Cash freed by DSO improvement = (8 / 365) x 110,000,000\n8 x 110,000,000 = 880,000,000\n880,000,000 / 365:\n  365 x 2,410,958 = 879,999,670\n  remainder = 330 -> 330/365 \u2248 0.904\nCash freed \u2248 2,410,958.90\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dso_days\": 49.92,\n  \"dio_days\": 64.21,\n  \"dpo_days\": 47.08,\n  \"cash_conversion_cycle_days\": 67.05,\n  \"cash_freed_by_dso_improvement\": 2410958.90\n}\n```\n", "trial": 0}
{"task_id": "board-memo-001", "category": "strategic_narrative", "difficulty": "medium", "model": "claude-fable-5 (subagent harness)", "mode": "chat", "score": 1.0, "parsed": true, "error": null, "fields": [], "judge_notes": "[{\"name\": \"Numeric accuracy\", \"max_points\": 5, \"points\": 5, \"note\": \"All figures check out against the data: revenue $15,897K vs $17,200K plan (-$1,303K, 7.6%), opex $6,750K vs $7,150K (-$400K, 5.6%), EMEA $6,150K vs $7,500K (-$1,350K, 18%), NA +$87K, APAC -$40K, R&D $2,914K vs $3,350K (-$436K, 13%), S&M +$6K, G&A +$30K, cash $38,000K. No fabricated figures; the '3-4 roadmap-critical hires' is a prioritization recommendation within the stated 8 open roles, not an invented data point.\"}, {\"name\": \"Primary revenue driver\", \"max_points\": 4, \"points\": 4, \"note\": \"Correctly identifies the EMEA miss as the driver, quantifies it (-$1,350K, more than the total shortfall given NA's +$87K offset), and explicitly links it to the 3 churned EMEA enterprise logos, noting zero churn elsewhere.\"}, {\"name\": \"Opex favorability driver\", \"max_points\": 3, \"points\": 3, \"note\": \"Correctly attributes the $400K favorability to R&D underspend (-$436K) driven by the 8 unfilled headcount, and rightly frames it as a hiring shortfall rather than efficiency.\"}, {\"name\": \"Actionable recommendations\", \"max_points\": 3, \"points\": 3, \"note\": \"Recommendations are specific and tied directly to the drivers: 30-day churn post-mortem on the 3 lost EMEA logos with CRO-led Q4 save plan, NDR-driven expansion push, prioritized R&D hiring catch-up with contractor bridge and Q4 reforecast, and guidance reset. Not boilerplate.\"}, {\"name\": \"Board-appropriate communication\", \"max_points\": 3, \"points\": 3, \"note\": \"Leads with the headline vs-plan numbers, clear labeled structure (headline, revenue variance, opex variance, recommendations), approximately 370 words \\u2014 within the 400-word limit.\"}, {\"name\": \"Secondary KPI signal\", \"max_points\": 2, \"points\": 2, \"note\": \"Uses NDR of 101.8% substantively (thin expansion cushion, churn flows to top line) and cites the $38,000K cash balance to frame runway; both are integrated, not just mentioned.\"}]", "latency_s": null, "input_tokens": null, "output_tokens": null, "response_text": "FINANCE SECTION \u2014 Q3 BOARD MEMO\n\nHeadline: Q3 revenue was $15,897K against a plan of $17,200K \u2014 a miss of $1,303K, or 7.6% below plan. Opex came in at $6,750K versus a $7,150K budget, $400K (5.6%) favorable, but most of that \"savings\" is unintentional. Quarter-end cash was $38,000K.\n\nRevenue variance: the miss is an EMEA story. EMEA delivered $6,150K against a $7,500K plan \u2014 $1,350K (18%) below budget \u2014 which more than accounts for the total company shortfall. The other regions were essentially on plan: NA beat by $87K ($4,587K vs $4,500K) and APAC was $40K light ($5,160K vs $5,200K). The EMEA shortfall coincides with the churn of 3 enterprise logos in the region this quarter; no enterprise logos churned anywhere else. Net dollar retention of 101.8% confirms the pressure: we are barely expanding within the existing base, so churn of this size flows almost directly to the top line.\n\nOpex variance: the $400K underspend is concentrated in R&D, which spent $2,914K against a $3,350K budget \u2014 $436K (13%) under. This maps to the 8 open R&D headcount that remain unfilled; it is a hiring shortfall, not efficiency, and it carries product-delivery risk into future quarters. S&M ($2,156K vs $2,150K) and G&A ($1,680K vs $1,650K) were on budget, with G&A modestly over by $30K.\n\nRecommendations:\n1. Stabilize EMEA retention now. Commission a churn post-mortem on the 3 lost enterprise logos within 30 days, put executive sponsors and success plans on the remaining at-risk EMEA enterprise accounts, and have the CRO present a Q4 EMEA save/expansion plan to the board.\n2. Rebuild expansion motion. With NDR at 101.8%, fund a targeted upsell/cross-sell push into the installed base \u2014 this is the fastest path to closing the revenue gap without new-logo dependence.\n3. Close the R&D hiring gap deliberately. Treat the 8 open roles as a delivery risk: prioritize the 3-4 most roadmap-critical hires, consider contractors to bridge, and reforecast Q4 R&D spend so the \"favorable\" variance does not mask slipping commitments.\n4. Reset Q4 guidance. Re-plan Q4 revenue with EMEA at a realistic run-rate rather than the original plan, and hold the opex line elsewhere; with $38,000K of cash, we have runway to fix the drivers rather than cut into them.\n", "trial": 0}
